1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,365
Welcome to WorkPulse, powered by AI.

2
00:00:02,415 --> 00:00:03,974
Smarter workforce, better business.

3
00:00:04,024 --> 00:00:10,011
In this tutorial you will learn how to use
WorkPulse from beginning to end: setting

4
00:00:10,061 --> 00:00:14,840
up your organization, inviting your team,
tracking time with the desktop app,

5
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,462
approving timesheets, billing your
clients, running payroll, getting the

6
00:00:18,512 --> 00:00:23,694
reports you need, and letting WorkPulse AI
point out what needs your attention.

7
00:00:23,744 --> 00:00:28,523
Everything you see is the real
application, running with a demo company

8
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:32,950
called Northwind Creative, so you can
follow along step by step.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,362
WorkPulse has three kinds of users.

10
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:42,185
Administrators and managers use this web
app to organize people and projects,

11
00:00:42,235 --> 00:00:44,999
approve time, and handle billing and
payroll.

12
00:00:45,049 --> 00:00:50,626
Workers, the people whose time is tracked,
use the WorkPulse desktop app on Windows,

13
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:51,832
macOS or Linux.

14
00:00:51,882 --> 00:00:57,862
It tracks their time and shows them their
own timesheet, time off and pay stubs.

15
00:00:57,912 --> 00:01:03,891
And your clients can get a read-only
client portal that shows the work done for

16
00:01:03,941 --> 00:01:05,499
them, without any money.

17
00:01:05,549 --> 00:01:11,126
What each person sees depends on their
role, so two people can see different

18
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:11,528
menus.

19
00:01:11,578 --> 00:01:15,950
That is normal, and we will come back to
it later.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,839
The menu on the left follows the way work
flows through WorkPulse.

21
00:01:22,889 --> 00:01:26,098
You set up the organization and invite
people.

22
00:01:26,148 --> 00:01:29,765
You organize the work into clients,
projects and tasks.

23
00:01:29,815 --> 00:01:31,394
Your team tracks time.

24
00:01:31,444 --> 00:01:33,431
Managers review and approve it.

25
00:01:33,481 --> 00:01:35,876
Approved time becomes invoices and
payroll.

26
00:01:35,926 --> 00:01:41,580
Reports and AI Insights turn it all into
insight, and Performance shows how people

27
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:43,209
and teams are doing.

28
00:01:43,259 --> 00:01:48,913
This tutorial follows the same order, and
the chapter list in the description lets

29
00:01:48,963 --> 00:01:50,950
you jump to any part.

30
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,750
To start using WorkPulse, create your
organization.

31
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:05,550
Enter your name, the name of your company,
your work email and a password of at least

32
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,150
ten characters, then type it again to
confirm it.

33
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,750
Then click Create organization.

34
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:15,550
You are the owner of this new
organization, and WorkPulse takes you

35
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,150
straight to the Overview.

36
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:22,350
For a new organization, the Overview shows
a Getting started checklist with five

37
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:27,950
steps: invite your team, create a project,
set pay and bill rates, connect the

38
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,750
desktop app, and review what is tracked.

39
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:36,750
Each step links to the right page, and it
ticks itself off as you go.

40
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,950
You can hide the checklist at any time.

41
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,593
Next time, sign in from the Welcome Back
page.

42
00:02:45,643 --> 00:02:51,260
If you forget your password, click Forgot
password, enter your work email and click

43
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,474
Send reset link.

44
00:02:52,524 --> 00:02:56,521
WorkPulse emails you a link to choose a
new password.

45
00:02:56,571 --> 00:03:02,998
For your privacy, the message is the same
whether or not the address has an account.

46
00:03:03,048 --> 00:03:07,045
Back on the sign-in page, enter your email
and password.

47
00:03:07,095 --> 00:03:11,498
The eye button shows the password so you
can check it.

48
00:03:11,548 --> 00:03:15,950
Click Sign in, and WorkPulse opens the
organization you used last.

49
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,409
When someone invites you to their
organization, you receive an invitation

50
00:03:22,459 --> 00:03:22,815
link.

51
00:03:22,865 --> 00:03:24,842
Opening it shows this page.

52
00:03:24,892 --> 00:03:30,923
Check your name, choose a password, type
it again to confirm it, and click Join

53
00:03:30,973 --> 00:03:31,328
organization.

54
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:35,788
Managers and administrators land in the
web app, ready to work.

55
00:03:35,838 --> 00:03:41,464
Workers are taken to a page where they
download the desktop app instead, because

56
00:03:41,514 --> 00:03:44,301
that is where they track their time.

57
00:03:44,351 --> 00:03:47,950
You will see that page in the desktop
chapter.

58
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,382
Protect your account with two-factor
sign-in.

59
00:03:52,432 --> 00:03:56,842
Open the account menu, choose Profile and
devices, and find Two-factor

60
00:03:56,892 --> 00:03:57,247
authentication.

61
00:03:57,297 --> 00:04:00,085
Click Set up and confirm your password.

62
00:04:00,135 --> 00:04:05,761
Scan the QR code with an authenticator app
on your phone, such as Google

63
00:04:05,811 --> 00:04:10,626
Authenticator or Microsoft Authenticator,
then type the six-digit code it shows and

64
00:04:10,676 --> 00:04:11,842
click Turn on.

65
00:04:11,892 --> 00:04:14,680
WorkPulse now gives you ten recovery
codes.

66
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:18,734
Each one works once, if you ever lose your
phone.

67
00:04:18,784 --> 00:04:24,004
Download them and keep them somewhere
safe, tick the box and click Done.

68
00:04:24,054 --> 00:04:28,869
From now on, signing in asks for a code
from your phone.

69
00:04:28,919 --> 00:04:34,139
Administrators can also require two-factor
for everyone, which we will see in the

70
00:04:34,189 --> 00:04:34,950
security chapter.

71
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,397
The Overview is your home page.

72
00:04:42,447 --> 00:04:46,474
It updates live, so you always see the
current picture.

73
00:04:46,524 --> 00:04:52,183
At the top, This month shows the time
logged, the estimated pay, the billable

74
00:04:52,233 --> 00:04:55,037
time and the estimated amount to bill.

75
00:04:55,087 --> 00:05:00,338
Estimates come from your rates and become
final once the time is approved.

76
00:05:00,388 --> 00:05:05,232
Worked today shows how much your team has
tracked so far today.

77
00:05:05,282 --> 00:05:10,533
Waiting for approval counts the timesheets
and manual time requests that need your

78
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:15,018
decision, and Project budgets warns you
before a project runs over.

79
00:05:15,068 --> 00:05:20,727
The switch at the top right changes whose
numbers you see: everyone, only yourself,

80
00:05:20,777 --> 00:05:21,950
or one member.

81
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,399
You can arrange the Overview to suit the
way you work.

82
00:05:28,449 --> 00:05:29,208
Click Customize.

83
00:05:29,258 --> 00:05:36,085
Every card now has controls to change its
size, move it up or down, or hide it.

84
00:05:36,135 --> 00:05:42,557
Hidden cards wait in the Hidden widgets
panel, so you can add them back at any

85
00:05:42,607 --> 00:05:42,961
time.

86
00:05:43,011 --> 00:05:48,624
There are cards for the current timer, who
is working, recent screenshots, time off,

87
00:05:48,674 --> 00:05:51,051
attendance, invoices, weekly limits and
more.

88
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:55,096
When you are happy with the layout, click
Save layout.

89
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:59,950
Each person has their own layout, and
Reset brings back the default.

90
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,843
The sidebar groups the pages by job: Time
Tracking, Workforce, Project Management,

91
00:06:06,893 --> 00:06:11,329
Finance, Reports and Performance, with
Settings and Help at the bottom.

92
00:06:11,379 --> 00:06:13,775
Click a group to open it.

93
00:06:13,825 --> 00:06:17,037
At the top left is the organization
switcher.

94
00:06:17,087 --> 00:06:22,338
If you belong to more than one
organization, switch between them here, or

95
00:06:22,388 --> 00:06:23,969
create a new one.

96
00:06:24,019 --> 00:06:29,678
At the top right, the bell shows your
notifications, such as a timesheet waiting

97
00:06:29,728 --> 00:06:32,533
for approval or a time off request.

98
00:06:32,583 --> 00:06:35,387
Click Mark all read to clear them.

99
00:06:35,437 --> 00:06:41,503
Next to it is your account menu, with your
profile and devices, what is monitored,

100
00:06:41,553 --> 00:06:43,950
and the light and dark themes.

101
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,374
Whenever you are unsure, open Help.

102
00:06:48,424 --> 00:06:52,819
The Help Center is a plain-language manual
for the whole app.

103
00:06:52,869 --> 00:06:58,475
Search for what you want to do, for
example invoice, and open a guide.

104
00:06:58,525 --> 00:07:04,132
Each guide gives you numbered steps, with
buttons that take you straight to the

105
00:07:04,182 --> 00:07:04,940
right page.

106
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:09,384
Many pages also have their own Help link
at the top.

107
00:07:09,434 --> 00:07:12,617
If you are new, click Start the tour.

108
00:07:12,667 --> 00:07:17,061
It highlights each part of the screen with
a short explanation.

109
00:07:17,111 --> 00:07:21,506
Use Next to move on, or Skip tour to close
it.

110
00:07:21,556 --> 00:07:25,950
The tour starts by itself the first time
you sign in.

111
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,750
Now let us set up the organization.

112
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,950
Open Settings in the menu on the left.

113
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:42,550
It lists every settings page, and you only
see the ones your role allows.

114
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:47,750
On the Organization page, the General
panel sets your company name, time zone,

115
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:52,550
the day your week starts, your currency,
and how durations are shown.

116
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:57,750
The Company profile below holds your logo,
tax ID, address and contact details.

117
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:00,950
They appear on your invoices and pay
stubs.

118
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:06,550
For those documents you can also upload a
Logo on documents: any shape, never

119
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:09,750
cropped, so a wide logo keeps its
proportions.

120
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:14,950
Further down, Client folders lets you
organize projects by client; you will see

121
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,550
it in chapter six.

122
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,950
After a change, click Save changes.

123
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,950
The Time and pay page controls how time
becomes pay.

124
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,750
The timesheet period sets how often
members submit their time, for example

125
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,550
every week.

126
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:36,550
Timesheet rules can lock old time so it
cannot be changed, set minimum hours, and

127
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,550
remind people about missing time.

128
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:44,550
Below are the overtime rules and your time
types, such as regular or overtime, each

129
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:47,350
with its own pay and bill multiplier.

130
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:50,950
Break types define the breaks your people
can take.

131
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:58,150
Let us add a coffee break: name it Coffee,
make it a paid break, with a maximum of

132
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:58,950
fifteen minutes.

133
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,550
And a lunch break: unpaid, up to sixty
minutes.

134
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:06,950
We will plan these breaks on a project in
a moment.

135
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,162
Tracking policies decide what the desktop
app records.

136
00:09:12,212 --> 00:09:14,570
The organization default applies to
everyone.

137
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:21,395
A timer started in the desktop app counts
once the app confirms it is running; if it

138
00:09:21,445 --> 00:09:26,213
does not confirm in time, the timer stops
and adds no time.

139
00:09:26,263 --> 00:09:30,227
Activity counts keyboard and mouse use,
never the keys themselves.

140
00:09:30,277 --> 00:09:35,446
Idle detection asks people what to do with
time when they step away.

141
00:09:35,496 --> 00:09:41,468
Screenshots can be switched on, taken a
set number of times every ten minutes, and

142
00:09:41,518 --> 00:09:41,870
blurred.

143
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:45,884
Apps and URLs record which applications
and websites are used.

144
00:09:45,934 --> 00:09:50,702
You can override any setting for a team or
for one member.

145
00:09:50,752 --> 00:09:54,315
Here, the Client Success team has its
screenshots blurred.

146
00:09:54,365 --> 00:09:57,125
An overridden setting shows Reset to
inherited.

147
00:09:57,175 --> 00:10:02,746
When you save, the affected members are
notified, and each member can always see

148
00:10:02,796 --> 00:10:03,950
what is monitored.

149
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,150
Roles control who can see and do what.

150
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:13,950
WorkPulse comes with built-in roles:
System Admin for full access, Team Manager

151
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:19,550
for running teams and projects without the
money settings, and Worker for people who

152
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,350
track time.

153
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:23,550
The matrix shows every permission for
every role.

154
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:27,550
If you need something in between, create a
custom role.

155
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:33,150
Give it a name, start from an existing
role, and then adjust its permissions.

156
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:37,950
Each permission can apply to the person
themselves, their assigned projects, their

157
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,950
team, or the whole organization.

158
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,375
To add people, open Workforce, then
Members, and click Invite member.

159
00:10:49,425 --> 00:10:53,398
Enter their email address and name, and
choose a role.

160
00:10:53,448 --> 00:10:55,812
Most people you track are Workers.

161
00:10:55,862 --> 00:11:02,249
You can also put them in teams and give
them projects right away, so everything is

162
00:11:02,299 --> 00:11:03,858
ready when they join.

163
00:11:03,908 --> 00:11:05,065
Click Send invitation.

164
00:11:05,115 --> 00:11:06,674
WorkPulse emails the invitation.

165
00:11:06,724 --> 00:11:13,111
If the email cannot be sent, the dialog
shows the invitation link so you can share

166
00:11:13,161 --> 00:11:13,916
it yourself.

167
00:11:13,966 --> 00:11:18,743
Until the person accepts, the invitation
waits under Pending invitations, where you

168
00:11:18,793 --> 00:11:19,950
can revoke it.

169
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,769
Click a member to open their profile.

170
00:11:24,819 --> 00:11:28,394
The Overview shows their details, quick
links and access.

171
00:11:28,444 --> 00:11:34,033
Here you can suspend or remove someone, or
reset their two-factor sign-in if they

172
00:11:34,083 --> 00:11:35,242
lose their phone.

173
00:11:35,292 --> 00:11:38,464
Personal info holds HR details and private
notes.

174
00:11:38,514 --> 00:11:43,297
The other tabs show the member's time,
activity, projects, the computers they

175
00:11:43,347 --> 00:11:48,533
use, and the tracking policy that applies
to them, combined from the organization,

176
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:50,950
their team and any personal overrides.

177
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,382
Teams group people who work together.

178
00:11:55,432 --> 00:12:02,274
On the Teams tab, click New team, give it
a name and a description, and click Create

179
00:12:02,324 --> 00:12:02,680
team.

180
00:12:02,730 --> 00:12:03,896
Then add people.

181
00:12:03,946 --> 00:12:09,166
A team member with the Manager role
approves the team's timesheets and time

182
00:12:09,216 --> 00:12:12,409
off, and sees the team's time and
activity.

183
00:12:12,459 --> 00:12:18,491
Here, Priya becomes the manager of the new
Video Production team, and Kenji joins as

184
00:12:18,541 --> 00:12:19,301
a member.

185
00:12:19,351 --> 00:12:22,950
A person can belong to more than one team.

186
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,950
Work in WorkPulse is organized into
clients, projects and tasks.

187
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,550
Start with the client.

188
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:37,150
Open Project Management, then Clients, and
click New client.

189
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:40,350
Enter the company name and a contact
person.

190
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,550
The contact email is where invoices are
sent.

191
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:49,150
Choose the client's currency, and if you
charge this client a standard hourly rate,

192
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,350
enter it here.

193
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:56,750
You can also add a logo, a colour and the
language for documents such as invoices.

194
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,950
Click Create client.

195
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,971
Sometimes a client is created by mistake,
for example twice.

196
00:13:04,021 --> 00:13:07,589
A client that was never used can be
deleted.

197
00:13:07,639 --> 00:13:10,404
Open its actions menu and choose Delete.

198
00:13:10,454 --> 00:13:15,228
WorkPulse explains what will be removed:
the client with its projects, tasks,

199
00:13:15,278 --> 00:13:17,239
rates, budgets and portal access.

200
00:13:17,289 --> 00:13:22,465
Deleting only works for a client with no
invoices, payments, expenses or tracked

201
00:13:22,515 --> 00:13:24,878
time, and it cannot be undone.

202
00:13:24,928 --> 00:13:28,898
For a client you have worked with, use
Archive instead.

203
00:13:28,948 --> 00:13:34,125
Archiving hides the client and its
projects but keeps all its history, and

204
00:13:34,175 --> 00:13:36,136
you can restore it later.

205
00:13:36,186 --> 00:13:38,950
Tick Show archived to see archived
clients.

206
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:46,217
Clients can follow the work you do for
them in a client portal.

207
00:13:46,267 --> 00:13:49,053
From the client's actions, open Client
portal.

208
00:13:49,103 --> 00:13:55,131
Switch the portal on and choose what the
client sees: hours per person, task and

209
00:13:55,181 --> 00:13:59,588
day, task progress and hour budgets,
activity levels, and even screenshots

210
00:13:59,638 --> 00:14:01,209
taken on their projects.

211
00:14:01,259 --> 00:14:05,666
You can also add a short summary written
by WorkPulse AI.

212
00:14:05,716 --> 00:14:11,338
It uses only the progress the client
already sees, never money, hours or names,

213
00:14:11,388 --> 00:14:14,579
and is written at most once a day.

214
00:14:14,629 --> 00:14:16,605
The portal never shows money.

215
00:14:16,655 --> 00:14:21,062
Click Preview as client to see exactly
what they will see.

216
00:14:21,112 --> 00:14:25,114
To give someone access, enter their email
and click Invite.

217
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:27,950
You can revoke access at any time.

218
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,799
Next, create a project for the client.

219
00:14:32,849 --> 00:14:35,241
Open Projects and click New project.

220
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:38,497
Give it a name and choose the client.

221
00:14:38,547 --> 00:14:45,008
Add start and end dates and an estimate of
the hours, so WorkPulse can show progress

222
00:14:45,058 --> 00:14:46,229
against the plan.

223
00:14:46,279 --> 00:14:51,113
Then choose who works on it, either
individual members or whole teams.

224
00:14:51,163 --> 00:14:55,590
Members only see and track the projects
they are assigned to.

225
00:14:55,640 --> 00:15:02,915
In the finance section you can set pay and
bill rates for this project, or mark it as

226
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:03,729
not billable.

227
00:15:03,779 --> 00:15:04,950
Click Create project.

228
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,046
For projects with a regular rhythm, you
can plan breaks.

229
00:15:11,096 --> 00:15:14,733
Open the project and go to its Settings
tab.

230
00:15:14,783 --> 00:15:21,287
In the Breaks section, click Add break,
choose a break type and, if you like, a

231
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:22,926
time and a length.

232
00:15:22,976 --> 00:15:29,890
Here we plan a fifteen minute coffee break
at ten thirty, and an hour for lunch at

233
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:30,299
twelve.

234
00:15:30,349 --> 00:15:31,528
Click Save changes.

235
00:15:31,578 --> 00:15:37,263
People on this project now see these
breaks as one-tap buttons in the desktop

236
00:15:37,313 --> 00:15:40,950
app, with a reminder when a break is due.

237
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,213
Tasks break a project into pieces of work.

238
00:15:46,263 --> 00:15:48,661
Open Tasks and click New task.

239
00:15:48,711 --> 00:15:55,187
Choose the project, give the task a title,
and set its status, priority, due date and

240
00:15:55,237 --> 00:15:56,818
an estimate in hours.

241
00:15:56,868 --> 00:15:59,674
Assign it to one or more people.

242
00:15:59,724 --> 00:16:06,200
When they track time, they can pick the
task, so you see exactly where the hours

243
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:06,608
went.

244
00:16:06,658 --> 00:16:13,542
Filter the list by project or status, or
switch on Assigned to me to see your own

245
00:16:13,592 --> 00:16:13,950
work.

246
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,178
With many clients, the project list gets
long.

247
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:24,827
Once folders are switched on in Settings,
the Projects page gets a second view.

248
00:16:24,877 --> 00:16:29,266
Choose Client folders, then click New
folder and pick the client.

249
00:16:29,316 --> 00:16:34,915
A folder simply shows all of that client's
projects together: nothing is copied or

250
00:16:34,965 --> 00:16:35,318
moved.

251
00:16:35,368 --> 00:16:36,529
Open the folder.

252
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:41,775
Each project opens up to show its status,
task progress, team members, milestones

253
00:16:41,825 --> 00:16:42,582
and dates.

254
00:16:42,632 --> 00:16:48,231
Revision history shows every change made
to the project: who changed what, the old

255
00:16:48,281 --> 00:16:51,055
and new values, and the reason given.

256
00:16:51,105 --> 00:16:57,108
From the folder's actions you can also add
existing projects that have no client yet.

257
00:16:57,158 --> 00:17:01,950
Renaming or archiving a folder never
changes the client or its projects.

258
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,186
Now let us switch to the worker's side.

259
00:17:10,236 --> 00:17:13,017
Workers use WorkPulse through the desktop
app.

260
00:17:13,067 --> 00:17:17,062
After accepting an invitation, they land
on this download page.

261
00:17:17,112 --> 00:17:22,321
It offers the right installer for their
computer: Windows, macOS, or Ubuntu and

262
00:17:22,371 --> 00:17:22,725
Debian.

263
00:17:22,775 --> 00:17:24,343
Click the download button.

264
00:17:24,393 --> 00:17:30,815
A short guide opens with the install
steps, and a link to the full setup guide

265
00:17:30,865 --> 00:17:33,242
with a picture for each step.

266
00:17:33,292 --> 00:17:38,905
On Windows, for example, if Windows
protects your PC, click More info and then

267
00:17:38,955 --> 00:17:39,714
Run anyway.

268
00:17:39,764 --> 00:17:42,950
The app updates itself automatically from
then on.

269
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:50,950
Open WorkPulse on your computer and sign
in with the same email and password you

270
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,150
use for WorkPulse.

271
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:55,750
You can also sign in through your browser
instead.

272
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:59,750
If your organization requires it, an
administrator approves new computers

273
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,750
before they can track time.

274
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:08,150
Once you are signed in, the menu on the
left takes you to everything you need:

275
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:12,150
Home, Track, Timesheet, Time off,
Schedule, Pay stubs and Settings.

276
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,950
The app only shows your own data.

277
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,161
This is Home.

278
00:18:18,211 --> 00:18:22,198
To start work, choose a project, then
click Clock in.

279
00:18:22,248 --> 00:18:26,234
The timer starts and the status changes to
Clocked in.

280
00:18:26,284 --> 00:18:32,289
You can also choose a task, and change
project at any time with the Change

281
00:18:32,339 --> 00:18:32,693
button.

282
00:18:32,743 --> 00:18:39,152
Below the timer are the breaks planned for
this project, the ones we set up earlier,

283
00:18:39,202 --> 00:18:40,767
ready as one-tap buttons.

284
00:18:40,817 --> 00:18:46,418
Add a short work note so your manager
knows what you are working on.

285
00:18:46,468 --> 00:18:52,473
On the right, Today's summary shows your
tracked time today and this week, how much

286
00:18:52,523 --> 00:18:54,491
was active, and your shift.

287
00:18:54,541 --> 00:19:00,143
If your organization records activity, it
is shown here too, so nothing is hidden

288
00:19:00,193 --> 00:19:00,950
from you.

289
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:06,601
When it is time for a break, tap it.

290
00:19:06,651 --> 00:19:10,658
WorkPulse pauses your time and shows how
long is left.

291
00:19:10,708 --> 00:19:17,554
When a planned break is due, the app
reminds you, and if a break runs long, it

292
00:19:17,604 --> 00:19:20,393
tells you how far over you are.

293
00:19:20,443 --> 00:19:23,639
When you are back, click Clock back in.

294
00:19:23,689 --> 00:19:29,318
If you step away from the computer without
taking a break, WorkPulse notices that

295
00:19:29,368 --> 00:19:32,158
there was no keyboard or mouse activity.

296
00:19:32,208 --> 00:19:36,620
When you return, it asks what to do with
that time.

297
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:42,299
Keep it if you were working, for example
in a meeting, or discard it.

298
00:19:42,349 --> 00:19:45,950
If you do not answer, your organization's
default applies.

299
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,593
At the end of the day, click Clock out.

300
00:19:51,643 --> 00:19:56,450
WorkPulse asks for a short end-of-day
report: what you completed, and whether

301
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:58,069
the work is finished.

302
00:19:58,119 --> 00:20:01,712
Your manager reads these reports in the
web app.

303
00:20:01,762 --> 00:20:08,188
The report is saved on your computer
first, so it is never lost, even when you

304
00:20:08,238 --> 00:20:08,998
are offline.

305
00:20:09,048 --> 00:20:11,021
Click Submit and clock out.

306
00:20:11,071 --> 00:20:17,093
In fact, if your internet connection drops
at any time, the app keeps tracking and

307
00:20:17,143 --> 00:20:19,926
sends everything when you are back online.

308
00:20:19,976 --> 00:20:21,950
No tracked time is lost.

309
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,550
Track holds your work.

310
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:30,750
Projects lists everything you are assigned
to; click one to start tracking it.

311
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:36,350
Tasks shows your tasks, and you can start
the timer straight from a task.

312
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:40,350
Sessions lists the time you tracked over
the last days.

313
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:45,550
Forgot to start the timer, for example
during a call on your phone?

314
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:51,150
Click Add manual time, choose the project
and the time, and give a reason.

315
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:56,350
Depending on your organization, manual
time is added straight away or sent to

316
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,950
your manager for approval.

317
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:05,664
Timesheet shows your time for the current
period, with the hours for each day.

318
00:21:05,714 --> 00:21:09,338
Use Previous and Next to look at other
periods.

319
00:21:09,388 --> 00:21:15,460
When the period is complete, click Submit
to send it to your manager for approval.

320
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:21,583
If your manager asks for changes, the
timesheet comes back to you and the Home

321
00:21:21,633 --> 00:21:24,032
page tells you what needs attention.

322
00:21:24,082 --> 00:21:29,338
Activity shows your own activity blocks
and the apps and websites that were

323
00:21:29,388 --> 00:21:32,195
recorded, exactly what your manager can
see.

324
00:21:32,245 --> 00:21:39,134
Reports gives you your worked hours by day
and by project for this week, last week or

325
00:21:39,184 --> 00:21:39,950
this month.

326
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:47,241
To ask for time off, open Time off and
click Request time off.

327
00:21:47,291 --> 00:21:53,345
Choose the type, the dates, and add a
reason if you like, then click Send

328
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:53,752
request.

329
00:21:53,802 --> 00:21:58,229
Your manager is notified, and you can
follow the request here.

330
00:21:58,279 --> 00:22:02,299
Schedule shows your working hours for this
week and next.

331
00:22:02,349 --> 00:22:08,403
Pay stubs lists your pay stubs once
payroll is finalized, each one with a PDF

332
00:22:08,453 --> 00:22:09,217
to download.

333
00:22:09,267 --> 00:22:14,915
Finally, Settings shows who you are signed
in as, your organization and this device,

334
00:22:14,965 --> 00:22:16,950
and lets you sign out.

335
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:27,231
Back in the web app, let us see the work
as it happens.

336
00:22:27,281 --> 00:22:29,263
Open Time Tracking, then Live.

337
00:22:29,313 --> 00:22:34,138
Who is working now shows everyone's
status, updated live: working, idle or

338
00:22:34,188 --> 00:22:40,231
paused, or offline, with the project they
are on and how long they have been

339
00:22:40,281 --> 00:22:40,638
working.

340
00:22:40,688 --> 00:22:43,888
Filter by status to focus on one group.

341
00:22:43,938 --> 00:22:49,169
From a member's actions you can open their
activity or their current session.

342
00:22:49,219 --> 00:22:54,044
And if someone forgot to stop their timer,
choose Force stop timer.

343
00:22:54,094 --> 00:23:00,138
The desktop app stops within about a
minute, and the change is recorded in the

344
00:23:00,188 --> 00:23:00,950
audit log.

345
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:08,728
Session history lists every work session:
who, on which project and task, where it

346
00:23:08,778 --> 00:23:13,680
was tracked from, when it started and
ended, and why it ended.

347
00:23:13,730 --> 00:23:16,569
Filter by date or member, or search.

348
00:23:16,619 --> 00:23:22,347
Click a session to see its details: the
time worked, each segment between pauses

349
00:23:22,397 --> 00:23:25,236
and breaks, and every change of state.

350
00:23:25,286 --> 00:23:28,950
From here you can jump to that day's
activity.

351
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:34,550
Activity shows how a day went, in
ten-minute blocks.

352
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,950
Choose a member and a day.

353
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:42,950
Each block shows the activity level, the
share of time with keyboard or mouse use,

354
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,550
and the screenshots taken, if your policy
records them.

355
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:48,950
Click a block for its details.

356
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,550
Use the activity filter to find quiet
periods quickly.

357
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:57,750
The Apps and URLs tabs show which
applications and websites were used, and

358
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:58,950
for how long.

359
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:03,750
Remember: keystrokes are only counted,
never recorded, and members see the same

360
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:04,950
information about themselves.

361
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:10,642
Remember the report Ava wrote when she
clocked out?

362
00:24:10,692 --> 00:24:13,104
Managers read them under End-of-day
reports.

363
00:24:13,154 --> 00:24:19,258
The summary shows how many reports came
in, from how many people, how many marked

364
00:24:19,308 --> 00:24:22,950
their work as finished, and the time they
cover.

365
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,001
Reports are grouped by day.

366
00:24:25,051 --> 00:24:29,104
Click one to read it in full, with its
session.

367
00:24:29,154 --> 00:24:34,847
Previous and Next move through the
reports, and Copy report puts the text on

368
00:24:34,897 --> 00:24:38,950
your clipboard, for example to paste into
a client update.

369
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:44,236
Monitoring works best when everyone knows
the rules.

370
00:24:44,286 --> 00:24:48,754
Every person can open What is monitored
from their account menu.

371
00:24:48,804 --> 00:24:54,093
It explains in plain language what is
recorded while they track time, which

372
00:24:54,143 --> 00:24:58,611
limits and time rules apply, and who can
see their data.

373
00:24:58,661 --> 00:25:03,539
Owners, administrators and managers are
not tracked unless you choose to track

374
00:25:03,589 --> 00:25:03,950
them.

375
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:12,569
Time entries is where you find and correct
time.

376
00:25:12,619 --> 00:25:18,197
Pick a date range, then filter by member,
client, project or task, or search.

377
00:25:18,247 --> 00:25:23,826
The totals at the bottom show the time
logged, billable time, and the estimated

378
00:25:23,876 --> 00:25:25,032
pay and billing.

379
00:25:25,082 --> 00:25:29,053
To correct an entry, open its actions and
choose Edit.

380
00:25:29,103 --> 00:25:33,476
Change what you need, and give a reason
for the change.

381
00:25:33,526 --> 00:25:39,105
Every change is kept: View history shows
each revision, who made it and why.

382
00:25:39,155 --> 00:25:45,136
You can also split an entry in two,
duplicate it, or select several entries to

383
00:25:45,186 --> 00:25:47,950
mark them billable or delete them
together.

384
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:56,021
Sometimes time needs to be added by hand,
for example a meeting away from the

385
00:25:56,071 --> 00:25:56,426
computer.

386
00:25:56,476 --> 00:26:02,902
Click Add time, choose the member and the
date, and enter either a duration or a

387
00:26:02,952 --> 00:26:04,521
start and end time.

388
00:26:04,571 --> 00:26:09,379
Choose the project and task, describe the
work and give a reason.

389
00:26:09,429 --> 00:26:15,045
Depending on your settings, the time goes
straight onto the timesheet, or it becomes

390
00:26:15,095 --> 00:26:17,474
a manual time request for approval.

391
00:26:17,524 --> 00:26:23,140
Members can also import time from a CSV
file on their timesheet, using the

392
00:26:23,190 --> 00:26:23,950
template provided.

393
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:29,588
When members submit their timesheets, they
arrive in Approvals.

394
00:26:29,638 --> 00:26:33,631
Click a timesheet to review the days,
projects and totals.

395
00:26:33,681 --> 00:26:36,056
If everything is right, click Approve.

396
00:26:36,106 --> 00:26:41,312
Approved time is final: it is what payroll
pays and what invoices bill.

397
00:26:41,362 --> 00:26:46,163
If something needs fixing, click Request
changes and explain what is wrong.

398
00:26:46,213 --> 00:26:50,205
The timesheet goes back to the member as a
draft.

399
00:26:50,255 --> 00:26:52,227
Reject works the same way.

400
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:58,290
To approve many at once, use the Approve
button at the top of the list.

401
00:26:58,340 --> 00:27:03,950
Below, manual time requests wait for the
same decision: approve or reject each one.

402
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:12,617
Team week gives you the whole team at a
glance: the hours each member worked on

403
00:27:12,667 --> 00:27:14,700
each day of the week.

404
00:27:14,750 --> 00:27:19,700
It is the quickest way to spot missing
days before you approve.

405
00:27:19,750 --> 00:27:25,533
Move between weeks with the arrows, and
select a row to open that member's

406
00:27:25,583 --> 00:27:25,950
timesheet.

407
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,950
Schedules hold everyone's working hours.

408
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:37,350
Open Workforce, then Schedules, to see the
week for each member.

409
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:40,150
To change someone's hours, open their
schedule.

410
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:46,950
Set the time zone, the date the new hours
start, and the start and end for each

411
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:47,750
working day.

412
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:52,950
Saving creates a new version, so past
attendance is still measured against the

413
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,350
hours that applied at the time.

414
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:58,950
Members see their own schedule in the
desktop app.

415
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,582
Attendance compares the schedule with the
time actually tracked.

416
00:28:04,632 --> 00:28:10,634
For each person you see whether they are
present, late, absent, on leave, on a

417
00:28:10,684 --> 00:28:12,652
holiday, or not started yet.

418
00:28:12,702 --> 00:28:19,108
Filter by status to follow up quickly, and
switch between a single day and the whole

419
00:28:19,158 --> 00:28:19,511
week.

420
00:28:19,561 --> 00:28:23,950
WorkPulse can also alert managers about
late starts and missed shifts.

421
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:30,397
Time off requests arrive under Time off,
on the Requests tab.

422
00:28:30,447 --> 00:28:34,439
Here is the request Ava sent from the
desktop app.

423
00:28:34,489 --> 00:28:40,099
Approve it, or reject it with a comment,
and she is notified straight away.

424
00:28:40,149 --> 00:28:43,333
The Calendar shows who is away and when.

425
00:28:43,383 --> 00:28:50,205
On Policies and holidays you set up the
kinds of time off, such as paid time off

426
00:28:50,255 --> 00:28:55,865
or sick leave: whether they are paid,
whether they need approval, and how much

427
00:28:55,915 --> 00:28:57,482
is earned each month.

428
00:28:57,532 --> 00:29:03,546
You can adjust a member's balance by hand,
and add public holidays, which are paid

429
00:29:03,596 --> 00:29:03,950
automatically.

430
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,363
Money in WorkPulse starts with rates.

431
00:29:11,413 --> 00:29:12,972
Open Finance, then Rates.

432
00:29:13,022 --> 00:29:16,591
Bill rates are what you charge clients per
hour.

433
00:29:16,641 --> 00:29:20,211
Pay rates are what you pay members per
hour.

434
00:29:20,261 --> 00:29:25,439
A rate can apply to the whole
organization, a client, a project, a

435
00:29:25,489 --> 00:29:30,667
member, or a member on one project, and
the most specific one wins.

436
00:29:30,717 --> 00:29:36,298
Rates are effective-dated: when a rate
changes, set the date it starts, and past

437
00:29:36,348 --> 00:29:38,309
time keeps its old rate.

438
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:44,743
Here we give the new Lumen project a bill
rate of one hundred and twenty-five per

439
00:29:44,793 --> 00:29:45,950
hour, from today.

440
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:52,873
Budgets warn you before a project or
client costs more than planned.

441
00:29:52,923 --> 00:29:57,796
Budgets shows how many are healthy, close
to the limit, or exceeded.

442
00:29:57,846 --> 00:30:04,771
Click Set budget, choose a project or a
client, and set the budget in hours or in

443
00:30:04,821 --> 00:30:05,181
money.

444
00:30:05,231 --> 00:30:09,694
It can run for the whole project or reset
every month.

445
00:30:09,744 --> 00:30:14,617
Warn at sets when WorkPulse alerts you,
for example at eighty percent.

446
00:30:14,667 --> 00:30:19,950
The same progress bars appear on the
Overview and in the client portal.

447
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:27,950
People can submit expenses with a receipt,
such as travel or software, and mark them

448
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:31,550
as billable to the client or to be
reimbursed.

449
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:36,350
Under Expenses, the Submitted tab holds
the ones waiting for a decision.

450
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:39,150
Check the receipt, then approve or reject.

451
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:42,350
Once you have paid someone back, click
Reimburse.

452
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:46,750
Approved billable expenses can be added to
the client's next invoice.

453
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:52,350
Like every finance list, Expenses has a
period filter and an Export button for

454
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:53,950
CSV, Excel or PDF.

455
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,362
Invoices turn billable time into money.

456
00:30:58,412 --> 00:31:03,187
The Invoices page shows what is
outstanding, what is overdue, your drafts,

457
00:31:03,237 --> 00:31:05,197
and what has been collected.

458
00:31:05,247 --> 00:31:06,404
Click New invoice.

459
00:31:06,454 --> 00:31:12,837
Choose the client and the period to bill,
and how to group the time: by project,

460
00:31:12,887 --> 00:31:14,043
task or member.

461
00:31:14,093 --> 00:31:18,465
You can include approved billable expenses
and set a tax rate.

462
00:31:18,515 --> 00:31:19,672
Click Preview lines.

463
00:31:19,722 --> 00:31:25,301
WorkPulse builds the lines from the
billable time and the bill rates, and you

464
00:31:25,351 --> 00:31:27,311
can add custom lines too.

465
00:31:27,361 --> 00:31:34,146
Then set the issue date, the due date and
a note, review the totals, and create the

466
00:31:34,196 --> 00:31:34,950
draft invoice.

467
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:42,950
On the invoice, Download PDF gives you the
finished document with your logo and the

468
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:43,750
client's details.

469
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:50,150
Click Send to email it to the client's
contact; if the client has no email, you

470
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:53,750
can mark it as sent and deliver it
yourself.

471
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:56,550
When the client pays, click Record
payment.

472
00:31:56,600 --> 00:32:02,550
Enter the amount, the date, the method and
a reference such as the transfer ID.

473
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:06,550
A payment can also be split across several
open invoices.

474
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:10,950
The invoice is now paid, and Payments
received lists every payment.

475
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,750
Payroll pays your people from approved
time.

476
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:20,950
First, pay groups set who is paid
together, how often, and in which

477
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:21,350
currency.

478
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:26,950
Then, on the Payrolls tab, click Run
payroll, choose the pay group and the

479
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:28,950
period, and create a draft.

480
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:33,350
WorkPulse calculates each person's pay
from their approved hours, overtime and

481
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:34,550
paid time off.

482
00:32:34,600 --> 00:32:37,350
Each approved hour is paid exactly once.

483
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:39,750
Add bonuses or deductions with Adjust.

484
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:46,550
If any approved time has no pay rate, the
payroll shows those hours and asks you to

485
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:51,750
confirm before it pays them at zero, so
set the missing rates first.

486
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:54,150
When everything is right, click Finalize.

487
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:58,150
Finalizing cannot be undone: corrections
go on the next payroll.

488
00:32:58,200 --> 00:33:00,950
Members can now see their pay stubs.

489
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:05,771
Each member's pay stub is a PDF.

490
00:33:05,821 --> 00:33:10,204
Members also find it in the desktop app,
under Pay stubs.

491
00:33:10,254 --> 00:33:14,234
Once the money has gone out, click Mark as
paid.

492
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:20,681
The Owed tab answers a different question:
how much do you owe each member for a

493
00:33:20,731 --> 00:33:21,890
period, right now?

494
00:33:21,940 --> 00:33:26,726
It shows tracked and approved time, and
the estimated and approved amounts.

495
00:33:26,776 --> 00:33:29,950
Estimated becomes approved once the
timesheets are approved.

496
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:38,150
For a quick answer, open Reports, then
Summary.

497
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:43,750
It shows the time logged, estimated pay,
billable time and estimated billing for a

498
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:46,950
period, together with average activity and
days off.

499
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:51,750
Switch between daily, weekly, fortnightly
and monthly periods, and step back with

500
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:52,550
the arrows.

501
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:58,950
Below are the hours per day, by client,
and by project, and a table with every

502
00:33:59,000 --> 00:33:59,750
person's totals.

503
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:04,950
Members who open Summary see only their
own time, and never any money.

504
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:12,613
The Report library is organized by the
question you want answered: where did time

505
00:34:12,663 --> 00:34:17,871
go, who was late or absent, which
timesheets are still pending, what is

506
00:34:17,921 --> 00:34:19,894
billable per client, and more.

507
00:34:19,944 --> 00:34:23,130
Open a report, for example Time and
activity.

508
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:29,197
Filter by date, members, teams, projects
or clients, and group the rows by up to

509
00:34:29,247 --> 00:34:32,433
three things, such as member, project and
client.

510
00:34:32,483 --> 00:34:36,074
Export downloads the result as CSV, Excel
or PDF.

511
00:34:36,124 --> 00:34:41,737
Large reports can be prepared in the
background, and you are notified when the

512
00:34:41,787 --> 00:34:42,950
file is ready.

513
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:48,642
If you need the same report regularly,
save it.

514
00:34:48,692 --> 00:34:51,924
Click Save report and give it a name.

515
00:34:51,974 --> 00:34:58,078
Choose a relative date range, such as last
month, so it always shows fresh numbers,

516
00:34:58,128 --> 00:35:03,412
and share it with everyone who can run the
report if you like.

517
00:35:03,462 --> 00:35:09,976
Switch on Email on a schedule, choose how
often and in which format, and add the

518
00:35:10,026 --> 00:35:10,386
recipients.

519
00:35:10,436 --> 00:35:12,847
WorkPulse now sends the report
automatically.

520
00:35:12,897 --> 00:35:16,950
Saved reports appear at the top of the
Report library.

521
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:27,550
Settings, Devices lists every computer
signed in to the desktop app: whose it is,

522
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:31,150
the operating system, the app version and
its status.

523
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:35,950
From a device's actions you can approve
it, when your organization requires

524
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,350
approval for new computers, ask for a new
sign-in, or revoke it, for example when a

525
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,550
laptop is lost.

526
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:47,150
A revoked device can no longer send any
data.

527
00:35:47,200 --> 00:35:49,950
Installing on many company computers at
once?

528
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:55,150
Under Enrollment tokens, create a token
and use it with the per-machine installer

529
00:35:55,200 --> 00:35:59,950
in Intune or Group Policy: those computers
join your organization already approved.

530
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:06,046
Under Security and retention you decide
how people sign in.

531
00:36:06,096 --> 00:36:10,962
Require two-factor authentication for
admins only or for everyone, set how long

532
00:36:11,012 --> 00:36:16,697
a session lasts, require approval for new
devices, and limit sign-in to your office

533
00:36:16,747 --> 00:36:18,745
networks with an IP allowlist.

534
00:36:18,795 --> 00:36:22,842
The data retention settings decide how
long data is kept.

535
00:36:22,892 --> 00:36:28,986
Access review then gives you a regular
check of who can do what: every active

536
00:36:29,036 --> 00:36:33,902
member, who still has no two-factor
sign-in, your roles and their permissions,

537
00:36:33,952 --> 00:36:35,950
and the active API keys.

538
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:43,992
Screenshots are kept for a set period,
thirty days by default, and older ones are

539
00:36:44,042 --> 00:36:46,006
deleted automatically on a schedule.

540
00:36:46,056 --> 00:36:50,839
Nothing is ever deleted until an
administrator previews what would go and

541
00:36:50,889 --> 00:36:51,644
approves it.

542
00:36:51,694 --> 00:36:56,881
Click Preview cleanup to see how many
screenshots would be deleted, then approve

543
00:36:56,931 --> 00:36:57,686
the cleanup.

544
00:36:57,736 --> 00:37:03,325
If you shorten the period later, the
approval is withdrawn and you are asked

545
00:37:03,375 --> 00:37:03,728
again.

546
00:37:03,778 --> 00:37:06,950
The history below shows every cleanup that
ran.

547
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:14,231
To connect WorkPulse to other systems,
such as accounting or HR software, create

548
00:37:14,281 --> 00:37:15,450
an API key.

549
00:37:15,500 --> 00:37:21,138
Give it a name, choose exactly what it may
access, and when it expires.

550
00:37:21,188 --> 00:37:25,200
The key is shown only once, so store it
safely.

551
00:37:25,250 --> 00:37:30,075
Webhooks work the other way around:
WorkPulse calls your system when something

552
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:33,325
happens, for example when a timesheet is
approved.

553
00:37:33,375 --> 00:37:36,575
Add the endpoint address and choose the
events.

554
00:37:36,625 --> 00:37:41,044
You can leave it switched off until your
system is ready.

555
00:37:41,094 --> 00:37:47,544
Each delivery is signed with a secret, so
your system can check it really comes from

556
00:37:47,594 --> 00:37:47,950
WorkPulse.

557
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:55,292
Finally, the audit log records every
important action: who did what, when, and

558
00:37:55,342 --> 00:37:56,114
to what.

559
00:37:56,164 --> 00:37:59,813
Earlier we deleted a client; here is that
action.

560
00:37:59,863 --> 00:38:06,388
Filter by action, by type, or by date, and
open an entry to see the details.

561
00:38:06,438 --> 00:38:12,553
The log cannot be changed, and you can
export it to CSV for your records.

562
00:38:12,603 --> 00:38:17,895
And for privacy requests, a member's
profile lets you export all of their

563
00:38:17,945 --> 00:38:19,950
personal data, or erase it.

564
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:31,014
Here is the same organization through the
eyes of Maya, who manages the Design team.

565
00:38:31,064 --> 00:38:34,652
Her Overview shows her team, not the whole
company.

566
00:38:34,702 --> 00:38:40,312
Her menu is shorter: she can approve her
team's timesheets and time off, watch

567
00:38:40,362 --> 00:38:46,780
their work, and manage the projects she is
assigned to, but she does not see rates,

568
00:38:46,830 --> 00:38:48,801
payroll or the organization settings.

569
00:38:48,851 --> 00:38:55,269
That is why two people can see different
menus, and why a page someone else talks

570
00:38:55,319 --> 00:38:57,695
about may be missing for you.

571
00:38:57,745 --> 00:39:02,950
If you need access to something, ask an
administrator to change your role.

572
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Performance shows how work is going,
measured from real outcomes.

573
00:39:12,050 --> 00:39:14,024
Open Performance, then Performance
overview.

574
00:39:14,074 --> 00:39:20,504
The organization score runs from 0 to 100
for the period you choose: a week, a

575
00:39:20,554 --> 00:39:22,933
month, a quarter or a year.

576
00:39:22,983 --> 00:39:29,413
Scores are calculated once a day, and each
page says when: Scores as of, then the

577
00:39:29,463 --> 00:39:29,818
time.

578
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:35,487
What the score is made of lists its five
parts: goal completion, project delivery,

579
00:39:35,537 --> 00:39:38,727
approved-work consistency, quality from
manager reviews, and attendance.

580
00:39:38,777 --> 00:39:44,801
A part with no data yet is left out, and
the others count for more.

581
00:39:44,851 --> 00:39:49,256
Activity levels, keystrokes and
screenshots are never part of a score.

582
00:39:49,306 --> 00:39:53,305
Click Scoring rules to decide how much
each part counts.

583
00:39:53,355 --> 00:39:56,950
The weights must add up to one hundred
percent.

584
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:03,412
Goals are measured from real work, so
nobody types progress in.

585
00:40:03,462 --> 00:40:06,658
Open Goals and challenges and click New
goal.

586
00:40:06,708 --> 00:40:13,959
Name the goal and choose who it is for: a
person, a team, a project or the whole

587
00:40:14,009 --> 00:40:14,365
organization.

588
00:40:14,415 --> 00:40:19,639
Choose how it is measured, such as tasks
completed, approved hours or work

589
00:40:19,689 --> 00:40:25,318
delivered on time, then set a target and
the dates, and click Save goal.

590
00:40:25,368 --> 00:40:28,563
From now on its progress updates by
itself.

591
00:40:28,613 --> 00:40:33,025
Under Achievements and recognition, people
earn badges automatically from their work,

592
00:40:33,075 --> 00:40:37,488
like Perfect Attendance or Project
Finisher, at bronze, silver, gold and

593
00:40:37,538 --> 00:40:38,299
platinum levels.

594
00:40:38,349 --> 00:40:41,950
Managers can also recognize someone,
always with a reason.

595
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:48,350
Leaderboards rank people by their
performance score, but only against others

596
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:53,950
in the same role family, so a designer is
never compared with an engineer.

597
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:57,150
Rankings never use hours, keyboard
activity or screenshots.

598
00:40:57,200 --> 00:41:03,150
Someone with too few approved days in the
period is scored, but not ranked yet.

599
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:06,750
Switch to Teams or Projects to compare
those instead.

600
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,750
Worker performance lists everyone's score.

601
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:15,950
Open a person to see what their score is
made of and how it has changed over time.

602
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:25,796
WorkPulse AI answers questions about how
WorkPulse works and about your own

603
00:41:25,846 --> 00:41:26,200
organization.

604
00:41:26,250 --> 00:41:29,027
Click Ask WorkPulse AI to open it.

605
00:41:29,077 --> 00:41:35,085
It suggests questions for the page you are
on, or you can type your own.

606
00:41:35,135 --> 00:41:40,335
Ask what needs your attention this week,
and it looks through approvals, budgets

607
00:41:40,385 --> 00:41:41,950
and attendance for you.

608
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:48,008
Ask how to do something, like approving a
timesheet, and it gives you the steps.

609
00:41:48,058 --> 00:41:52,046
WorkPulse AI only sees what you are
allowed to see.

610
00:41:52,096 --> 00:41:56,892
It can be wrong, so check important
figures on the page itself.

611
00:41:56,942 --> 00:42:02,950
Your conversations are kept under the chat
history, and New chat starts a fresh one.

612
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:09,440
AI Insights looks through your
organization's data and points out what

613
00:42:09,490 --> 00:42:10,256
needs attention.

614
00:42:10,306 --> 00:42:16,379
Every finding is measured from your own
data, labelled as a fact, a comparison or

615
00:42:16,429 --> 00:42:20,460
an estimate, and you only see what your
role allows.

616
00:42:20,510 --> 00:42:24,950
Choose a period, then a tab: workforce,
timesheets, projects, workflow, capacity

617
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:29,848
for the next two weeks, and finance for
people who handle money.

618
00:42:29,898 --> 00:42:36,787
Each finding says what was found, by how
much, and the next step, with a link to

619
00:42:36,837 --> 00:42:38,011
the right page.

620
00:42:38,061 --> 00:42:43,726
Click Explain with WorkPulse AI, and the
assistant explains the finding and what to

621
00:42:43,776 --> 00:42:44,950
do about it.

622
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,764
WorkPulse AI can also write for you.

623
00:42:49,814 --> 00:42:55,795
In a project or task, click Write with AI
under the description, and choose Draft

624
00:42:55,845 --> 00:42:57,404
from what WorkPulse knows.

625
00:42:57,454 --> 00:43:03,435
It writes a description from the project's
own facts, which are listed so you can

626
00:43:03,485 --> 00:43:04,239
check them.

627
00:43:04,289 --> 00:43:09,063
You can also rewrite text you typed,
shorter, longer or more professional.

628
00:43:09,113 --> 00:43:15,496
The draft only fills the field: edit it,
keep it or click Undo, and nothing is

629
00:43:15,546 --> 00:43:17,105
saved until you save.

630
00:43:17,155 --> 00:43:22,734
In AI Insights, Draft reminder writes a
friendly reminder for people who have not

631
00:43:22,784 --> 00:43:25,950
submitted their timesheet, ready for you
to send.

632
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:30,412
Notifications now come sorted by priority.

633
00:43:30,462 --> 00:43:35,335
Urgent and important ones are labelled,
and similar notifications are grouped, so

634
00:43:35,385 --> 00:43:39,437
ten devices going offline take one line
instead of ten.

635
00:43:39,487 --> 00:43:42,309
Open a group to see them all.

636
00:43:42,359 --> 00:43:48,053
To choose what you are told about, open
your account menu, then Profile and

637
00:43:48,103 --> 00:43:48,463
devices.

638
00:43:48,513 --> 00:43:54,206
Managers can switch on a weekly summary of
what needs their attention, written from

639
00:43:54,256 --> 00:43:59,950
AI Insights, so the most important things
reach you even when you are busy.

640
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:10,977
Let us finish with the questions people
ask most, all answered in the Help Center.

641
00:44:11,027 --> 00:44:14,191
Why are members sent to a download page?

642
00:44:14,241 --> 00:44:17,807
Because workers use the desktop app, not
the website.

643
00:44:17,857 --> 00:44:20,218
Can approved time still be changed?

644
00:44:20,268 --> 00:44:24,236
Yes: reopen the timesheet, correct it and
approve it again.

645
00:44:24,286 --> 00:44:30,664
Once its time is on an invoice, void the
invoice first; once it has been paid,

646
00:44:30,714 --> 00:44:35,084
correct it with a bonus or deduction on
the next payroll.

647
00:44:35,134 --> 00:44:37,896
What happens when a computer is offline?

648
00:44:37,946 --> 00:44:42,718
The app keeps tracking and sends
everything when it is back online.

649
00:44:42,768 --> 00:44:44,325
And are keystrokes recorded?

650
00:44:44,375 --> 00:44:44,727
No.

651
00:44:44,777 --> 00:44:47,539
WorkPulse only counts keyboard and mouse
activity.

652
00:44:47,589 --> 00:44:49,950
It never records what you type.

653
00:44:52,000 --> 00:44:53,958
Troubleshooting covers the usual problems.

654
00:44:54,008 --> 00:45:00,785
A member forgot to stop their timer: force
stop it from Live, then edit or split the

655
00:45:00,835 --> 00:45:02,391
entry in Time entries.

656
00:45:02,441 --> 00:45:08,013
A member's time is missing: check that
their app is online, since offline time

657
00:45:08,063 --> 00:45:12,832
arrives when they reconnect, and that
their computer is approved under Devices.

658
00:45:12,882 --> 00:45:16,848
For time they really did not track, add
manual time.

659
00:45:16,898 --> 00:45:22,470
The Approve button is greyed out: time was
added after the timesheet was submitted,

660
00:45:22,520 --> 00:45:26,485
so click Request changes and approve it
once they resubmit.

661
00:45:26,535 --> 00:45:32,509
And if a member does not have the latest
desktop app: updates download in the

662
00:45:32,559 --> 00:45:38,533
background and install when the member
quits the app from its icon in the system

663
00:45:38,583 --> 00:45:38,934
tray.

664
00:45:38,984 --> 00:45:42,950
Each guide links straight to the page that
fixes it.

665
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:50,350
Let us recap the whole journey.

666
00:45:50,400 --> 00:45:55,150
You created your organization and set the
rules for time and pay.

667
00:45:55,200 --> 00:46:00,350
You invited your people, organized them
into teams, and set up clients, projects

668
00:46:00,400 --> 00:46:01,150
and tasks.

669
00:46:01,200 --> 00:46:06,350
Workers tracked their time with the
desktop app, with breaks, idle checks and

670
00:46:06,400 --> 00:46:07,150
end-of-day reports.

671
00:46:07,200 --> 00:46:10,750
Managers watched the work, corrected time
and approved timesheets.

672
00:46:10,800 --> 00:46:16,350
And approved time became invoices and
payroll, with reports to tell you how it

673
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:17,150
all went.

674
00:46:17,200 --> 00:46:19,950
Everything comes together here on the
Overview.

675
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:23,550
Thank you for watching.

676
00:46:23,600 --> 00:46:28,750
Whenever you need a reminder, open Help
inside WorkPulse: every topic in this

677
00:46:28,800 --> 00:46:34,350
video has a step-by-step guide there, and
the product tour is one click away.

678
00:46:34,400 --> 00:46:36,350
Now it is your turn.

679
00:46:36,400 --> 00:46:37,950
Smarter workforce, better business.
